Docker on FenrirOS
==================

The packages are installed inert: nothing is enabled or started, and no user
is added to the `docker` group.

Rootful Docker
--------------
    dinitctl enable containerd
    dinitctl enable docker

The socket is /run/docker.sock, owned by root:docker. Membership in the
`docker` group gives root-equivalent access to the host; add a user only if
that is what you want:

    usermod -aG docker <user>

Optional settings go in /etc/docker/daemon.json (none is shipped; see
dockerd(8)). Docker uses iptables (or nftables with
"firewall-backend": "nftables") for container networking.

Rootless Docker
---------------
Needs /etc/subuid and /etc/subgid ranges for the user (rootlesskit,
slirp4netns or pasta). As that user:

    dockerd-rootless-setuptool.sh check
    dinitctl --user enable docker

and set DOCKER_HOST=unix://$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/docker.sock.

Plugins: docker-buildx (`docker buildx`, BuildKit) and docker-compose
(`docker compose`) are separate packages.
